# Test: IS-IS authentication config validation + $9$ secret handling (spec-isis-10).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-10-auth -- the authentication config surface reaches the
#            IS-IS YANG schema and validates: named key chains with key-id,
#            algorithm enum (cleartext / hmac-md5 / hmac-sha-256), $9$-encoded
#            secret, and the per-level (area/domain) and per-interface (circuit)
#            auth-key-chain references all validate through the real schema
#            (AC-5/AC-6/AC-7/AC-10/AC-11, User Story 5). A bad algorithm enum is
#            rejected before the engine builds the key store.
# PREVENTS:  regression where the key-chain schema is not wired (auth config
#            validates vacuously) or a plaintext secret leaks instead of $9$.
#
# Live sign-on-send / verify-on-receive, wrong-key rejection, hitless rotation,
# and FRR interop all need raw L2 (AF_PACKET) on a Linux veth: they are covered
# by the engine unit tests (auth_verify_test.go, auth_wiring_test.go,
# auth_keystore_test.go), the QEMU integration tests, and the FRR interop
# scenario `isis-auth-frr` (authored/run under spec-isis-13). This functional
# test exercises the config wiring only: config -> YANG schema -> key-chain
# validation -> $9$ secret decode.
#
# The two ze config-validate runs share one accumulated stdout in the .ci runner,
# so the INVALID case runs first (seq=1) and the VALID case last (seq=2): the
# final exit code asserted is the valid run's 0, and each run's distinct stdout
# marker is matched independently (rejection error + "configuration valid").

# --- Invalid algorithm enum: rejected by the YANG enumeration (seq=1). ---------
stdin=isis-auth-bad-algo:terminator=EOF_BAD
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	key-chains kc {
		key 1 {
			algorithm rot13
			secret x
		}
	}
}
EOF_BAD

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-auth-bad-algo:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=invalid value for algorithm

# --- Valid auth config: key chains, algorithms, $9$ secret, per-level/iface refs (seq=2) ---
stdin=isis-auth-valid:terminator=EOF_VALID
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	level l1-l2
	key-chains area-key {
		key 1 {
			algorithm hmac-sha-256
			secret $9$QI1cF39tpBEhrAtM87Nbw
		}
	}
	key-chains domain-key {
		key 1 {
			algorithm hmac-md5
			secret backbonepass
		}
	}
	key-chains iih-key {
		key 1 {
			algorithm cleartext
			secret hello123
		}
	}
	level-1 {
		auth-key-chain area-key
	}
	level-2 {
		auth-key-chain domain-key
	}
	interfaces {
		interface eth0 {
			circuit-type point-to-point
			level-1 {
				auth-key-chain iih-key
			}
			level-2 {
				auth-key-chain iih-key
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_VALID

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-auth-valid:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
